ARBORCORE CONFIG0-R0 SOURCE CONTRACT
====================================

STATUS
------
contract-version: 1
public-prefix: arbor_config
public-header: include/arborcore/config.h
production-source: src/c/config.c
static-archive: build/libarborcore_config0.a
archive-members: one exact CONFIG0 object
language: ISO C17
platform: generic C17; x86-64 GNU C layouts are reviewed evidence
stable-pre-1.0-binary-ABI: no

PUBLIC OPERATIONS
-----------------
arbor_config_measure:
  Validate the complete schema and all explicit sources, resolve every winner,
  and failure-atomically publish exact caller-storage requirements.

arbor_config_prepare:
  Repeat complete validation, prove capacity and alias conditions, then publish
  values, provenance, persistent UTF-8 bytes, and the result in schema order.

arbor_config_validate:
  Validate a prepared result against an independently supplied schema without
  source parsing, repair, allocation, I/O, or hidden process state.

SOURCE MODEL
------------
classes: DEFAULT, FILE, ENVIRONMENT, COMMAND_LINE
precedence: DEFAULT < FILE < ENVIRONMENT < COMMAND_LINE
discovery: none
file-I/O: none
getenv/environ/argc access: none
include-chain: none
duplicate semantic key within one class: error
unknown exact key: error
invalid higher override fallback: prohibited
lower-source error suppression: prohibited

SCHEMA MODEL
------------
abi-version: 1
schema-flags: zero
descriptor-flags: REQUIRED, HAS_DEFAULT, ALLOW_EMPTY
requirement: exactly one of REQUIRED and HAS_DEFAULT
allow-empty: UTF-8 only
namespaces: semantic, file, environment, command line
name-length: 1 through 63 bytes
name matching: exact ASCII bytes
enum matching: exact case-sensitive ASCII token
descriptor and enum order: caller supplied and immutable for each call
reserved fields: zero
inactive value fields: zero

GRAMMAR
-------
file record endings: LF or CRLF
terminal newline: optional
blank record: exactly zero bytes
comment: hash only in column zero
assignment delimiter: first equals byte
trimming: none
environment entry: NAME=VALUE
command-line entry: --NAME=VALUE
NUL, lone CR, and embedded line ending: error
quotes, escapes, interpolation, continuation, sections, arrays, nesting,
includes, heredocs, multiline values, shell rules, and locale rules: absent

TYPES
-----
BOOL: lowercase true or false only
U64: one or more ASCII decimal digits; checked full consumption
I64: optional minus and ASCII decimal digits; checked full consumption
UTF8: shortest-form Unicode scalar encoding, no NUL, no normalization
ENUM: one exact closed choice
floating point, units, bases, synonyms, coercions, and partial parsing: absent

MEASUREMENT
-----------
For N descriptors:
  descriptor_count  = N
  descriptor_bytes  = N * 184
  value_bytes       = N * 48
  provenance_bytes  = N * 24
  scratch_bytes     = N
  persistent_bytes  = sum of winning UTF-8 byte lengths
  result_bytes      = 48
All products, additions, pointer ranges, offsets, and capacities are checked.

OWNERSHIP AND PUBLICATION
-------------------------
allocation: zero
ownership transfer: zero
mutable global state: zero
result order: schema order
UTF-8 publication: copied into caller persistent storage
source lifetime: each measure or prepare call only
result lifetime: caller controlled
read-only input overlap: permitted
writable overlap: prohibited pairwise and against every nonempty input range
failure atomic outputs: requirements, result, values, provenance, persistent
scratch: only storage permitted to change before publication
extra-capacity writes: zero

PROVENANCE
----------
default: descriptor index, byte offset zero
file: physical zero-based record including ignored records; absolute value byte
environment: vector index; entry-relative value byte
command line: vector index; entry-relative value byte

DIAGNOSTICS
-----------
fields: code, source, record, byte offset, key index
failure codes: 23 exact plus NONE sentinel
raw source or value bytes: never
success write: none
failure publication: one complete diagnostic or none
first error order:
  schema, defaults, file, environment, command line, final required checks
printing, logging, exiting, telemetry: none

APPLICATION INTEGRATION
-----------------------
applications: HELLO0 and ECHO0
keys in order:
  template, bind_ipv4, port, backlog, event_wait_ms, drain_timeout_ms
legacy form: PROGRAM TEMPLATE PORT
named file acquisition: zero or one --config=PATH, application-owned
named environment selection: six exact ARBORCORE aliases
named command line: explicit CONFIG0 assignments only
resource order:
  configuration and numeric IPv4 validation before template, signals, HOST1,
  listener, and epoll publication
HOST1 mapping: existing options_make and open typed arguments only
HOST1 source or behavior change: prohibited

FROZEN EXCLUSIONS
-----------------
Assembly or ABI change: no
shared-library export: no
HOST1 reopen: no
HTTP, MVC, VIEW, runtime, or domain semantic change: no
database: no
runtime reload or watcher: no
remote configuration: no
DNS or wildcard exposure: no
JSON, YAML, TOML, INI, dotenv, or shell compatibility: no
IMAGE0 or Nonane implementation: no
new persistent dependency: no
